§ `s 3(1) -- who is next of kin, and who is senior (k097, d092)`

#ASSERT `Am I next of kin` `Ruby, Jake's daughter, 46` `k097: Jake at 72, on the Register since 2047, ventilated, brain death declared`
#ASSERT `Am I next of kin` `Chloe, Jake's sister, 76` `k097: Jake at 72, on the Register since 2047, ventilated, brain death declared`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I next of kin` `Tahlia, Jake's former wife, 72` `k097: Jake at 72, on the Register since 2047, ventilated, brain death declared`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I next of kin` `Jake, Chloe's brother, 14` `c026: Chloe at 18, on the Register, dies in hospital`
#ASSERT `Am I next of kin` `Sofia, Daniel's sister, 79` `d092: Daniel at 82, on the Register, the family confirms`

#ASSERT `Am I the senior available next of kin` `Ruby, Jake's daughter, 46` `k097: Jake at 72, on the Register since 2047, ventilated, brain death declared`
#ASSERT `Am I the senior available next of kin` `Chloe, Jake's sister, 76, consents` `Jake at 72, not on the Register, Ruby not available, Chloe consents`
#ASSERT `Am I the senior available next of kin` `Priya, Daniel's wife, 81, consents` `d092: Daniel at 82, on the Register, the family confirms`
#ASSERT `Am I the senior available next of kin` `Anjali, Daniel's daughter, 51, consents` `Daniel at 82, not on the Register, Priya not available, Anjali consents`
#ASSERT `Am I the senior available next of kin` `a de facto partner, 45, living with him, consents` `a man of 50, not on the Register, de facto partner consents, estranged wife objects`

§ `ss 22, 23 -- whose consent governs donation after death (c026, d021, k097, d092)`

-- c026 / d021: registering at 18 makes the deceased's own consent the governing one; without it, and without the senior
-- available next of kin's consent, there is no authority -- donation is not presumed.
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `c026: Chloe at 18, on the Register, dies in hospital` EQUALS `my own wish or consent, which no one else's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Chloe at 18, not on the Register, no one consents` EQUALS `no one's: there is no authority to remove my tissue`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Chloe at 18, not on the Register, both parents consent` EQUALS `my senior available next of kin's consent (s 22(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Chloe at 16, recorded wish to donate, dies in hospital` EQUALS `my own wish or consent, which no one else's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `k097: Jake at 72, on the Register since 2047, ventilated, brain death declared` EQUALS `my own wish or consent, which no one else's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Jake at 72, not on the Register, Ruby not available, Chloe consents` EQUALS `my senior available next of kin's consent (s 22(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Jake at 72, on the Register, a reportable death, no coroner's consent` EQUALS `no one's yet: the coroner must first consent (s 23)`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `d092: Daniel at 82, on the Register, the family confirms` EQUALS `my own wish or consent, which no one else's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Daniel at 82, on the Register, dies at home, not brought into hospital` EQUALS `no one's: there is no authority to remove my tissue`

